  "conditions": [
   "Hatching is blocked while the unit holds Item.EVIOLITE.",
   "The unit must still be on player.board when canEvolve runs (an egg/unit sold during the 2 s delay does not evolve).",
   "Only the Egg path adds BREEDER / GOLDEN_EGGS reductions (EGG_HATCH - 1); the 25 listed units are not eggs so the time is always EVOLVE_HATCH (5).",
   "The evolution target is pokemon.evolution unless a divergentEvolution function is declared on the rule; none of the 25 unit blocks declares one (not exhaustively verified beyond the evolution/evolutionRule lines).",
   "After evolve, EvolutionManager.afterEvolve updates synergies, runs the OnEvolution passive effects, handles the COSMOG / COSMOEM board units and calls tryEvolve again on the NEW unit. For a HATCH rule that retry is false: the new instance starts at stacks 0 and the hatch time is at least 4 (Egg 5, or 4 with BREEDER / GOLDEN_EGGS; every other HATCH unit 5), so a chained HATCH unit (for example Dreepy -> Drakloak) hatches again only after further stage-end increments. Probe: stacks 4 -> stage end -> 5 -> timer -> new instance with stacks 0 and no further timer.",
   "stacks counter: HatchEvolutionHandler.evolve sets the OLD instance's stacks to 0 before Player.transformPokemon (the comment says 'prevent trying to evolve twice in a row'); transformPokemon builds the new unit with PokemonFactory.createPokemonFromName, carries over permanent stat deltas and the TM (carryOverPermanentStats), dishes, position and items, and does not set stacks; the new instance keeps the field default 0 (pokemon.ts:103). The hatch of an Egg (not in scope) additionally rewards a golden-egg item when shiny.",
   "Delayed evolution window: updateHatch increments stacks, evaluates canEvolve and, if true, sets action HOP and schedules tryEvolve with setTimeout(…, 2000), a real-time server timer, not simulation time. tryEvolve re-checks canEvolve when it runs (Eviolite, still on the board, stacks >= required), so a unit sold during the window does not evolve; the board is not changed until the timer runs, and the stage-end loop over player.board therefore never visits the evolved instance in the same pass.",
   "Eviolite blocks hatching but not counting: a unit holding it keeps incrementing stacks at each stage end (probe: stacks 5 stay 5 with no timer) and can hatch later once the item is removed."
  ],
  "resetBehaviour": "The OLD instance's stacks is set to 0 on hatch; the NEW instance starts from the Pokemon field default (0) and receives only permanent stat deltas and the TM, not stacks. Otherwise the counter lives on the unit instance for the whole game (not per fight).",
